From edb77d6cf963c8e54f82889d5d5c79fcee7b4382 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <skoulik-claude@agentmail.to>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:00:56 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] metal: scale mul_mm swizzle group with src0 tile bytes

A fixed group of 8 row tiles is right for q8_0 and wrong for f16, whose src0
tile is ~2x the bytes. Measured on M1 Max at K=17408, N=5120, ubatch 2048:

  SWZ        2      4      8     16   (TFLOPS)
  q8_0    6.66   8.16   8.29   8.22
  f16     6.47   7.37   7.28   5.22

Both dtypes peak at ~9 MB of src0 held per group, so derive the group size from
NR0*nb01 instead of hardcoding a tile count. f16 at K=17408 goes 7.28 -> 7.34,
and the 29% cliff a fixed 16 would cause there cannot arise.

test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT passes 1154/1154 on MTL0.

Model: claude-opus-5
---
 ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal
index 2c5052831..dfb5b76f6 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal
@@ -10422,7 +10422,14 @@ kernel void kernel_mul_mm(
     int sx = tgpig.x;
 
     if ((size_t) args.ne1 * args.nb11 > (32u << 20)) {
-        constexpr int SWZ = 8;
+        // The group size follows the BYTES of a src0 tile rather than a fixed tile
+        // count, because the quantity being bounded is the SWZ*NR0 rows of src0 held
+        // across the group and an f16 tile is ~2x the bytes of a q8_0 one. Measured
+        // on M1 Max at K=17408: q8_0 peaks at 8 (8.29 TFLOPS) and f16 at 4 (7.37),
+        // and using 16 for f16 there costs 29%. Both optima sit at ~9 MB of src0,
+        // which is what this expression targets.
+        const uint tile_bytes = NR0*(uint) args.nb01;
+        const int  SWZ = (int) clamp((10u << 20)/max(tile_bytes, 1u), 1u, 16u);
 
         const int nbx = (args.ne1 + NR1 - 1)/NR1; // src1 (batch) tiles
         const int nby = (args.ne0 + NR0 - 1)/NR0; // src0 (row)   tiles
-- 
